### Five new-page proposals waiting on Karen

**A. `ingredients/cereals.md` — 8 sources** (EFSA cadmium 2009, EFSA lead 2010, EFSA nickel 2020, JECFA 73rd cadmium, Codex CXS 193-1995, Codex CCCF17 2024, altunay2023, nordberg2015)
"Cereals" is the agency matrix label for the full grain class (including rice). It differs from the existing `non-rice-grains.md`. Without this page, the wiki's most-cited regulatory opinions (EFSA, JECFA, Codex) can't route.

**B. `ingredients/breastmilk.md` — 6 sources** (atsdr-aluminum-2008, carignan2015, carignan2016, pikounis, soto-ocana2024, thoerig2025)
Human milk as the comparison matrix in formula-vs-breastfed infant exposure studies. Architecturally distinct from `milk-and-dairy.md` (bovine) and `infant-formula-ingredients.md`. Four are peer-reviewed cohort studies directly informing HMT&C infant formula thresholds.

**C. `ingredients/shellfish.md` — 6 sources** (efsa-cadmium-2009, fda-epa-fish-advice, jecfa-73rd-cadmium, nordberg2015, taylor2025, xia2025)
Shellfish = bivalves + crustaceans. Broader than existing `bivalve-molluscs.md`, narrower than `seafood.md`. FDA/EPA fish advice, EFSA, and JECFA all use this as a distinct regulatory matrix.

**D. `ingredients/freshwater-fish.md` — 9 sources** (auzier-guimaraes2025, jermilova2025, kovacik2024, lepak2025, naz2025, paul2025, rusko2026, sirisangarunroj2023, venant2025)
Freshwater fish have a distinct Hg/MeHg contamination profile driven by river mining runoff. All 9 papers study freshwater river or lake fish specifically; the mercury bioaccumulation drivers differ materially from marine fish.

**E. `ingredients/quinoa.md` — 6 sources** (bedoya-perales2023, ccopi2026, cr-fsasc2014, gul2024, roman-ochoa2021, rosales-huamani2023)
Quinoa has a well-characterized Cd accumulation problem tied to Andean mining soils. All commercial supply is Andean-origin. Codex set a specific Cd ML for quinoa at CCCF17 (2024) — it's a regulated matrix in its own right.
